WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:02.430
The phases are not the Earth's shadow.

00:03.130 --> 00:06.268
This is the Earth's shadow on the Moon, and it is rare.

00:06.718 --> 00:14.500
The Moon's path is tilted five degrees against ours, so at most full Moons it passes above or below the shadow.

00:14.950 --> 00:19.060
A few times a year they line up, and that is a lunar eclipse.
